.TH PLATFORM-POWER 1 "October 2026" "platform-power-manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
platform-power \- Dell Power Manager: thermal profile, battery charging and BIOS power settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B platform-power
[\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-minimized\fR] [\fIGTK/GApplication options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GTK4/libadwaita front-end for the \fBplatform-power-daemon\fR D-Bus service.
It shows and changes the ACPI platform profile, the battery charge
thresholds and (where the \fBdell-wmi-sysman\fR kernel driver exposes them)
Dell BIOS power settings, and provides a StatusNotifierItem tray icon.
.PP
The program never writes to sysfs itself: every change is sent to the
root-owned daemon over the system bus and authorized through polkit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the notification area (used by the autostart entry).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.nplacide95.PlatformPower.desktop
Autostart entry (starts the tray icon at login). Override or disable it
per user by copying it to \fI~/.config/autostart/\fR with
\fBHidden=true\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR busctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR pkaction (1)
.PP
Project documentation: /usr/share/doc/platform-power-manager/
